A||N||8||polomeno||Head Gasket Replacement help please !||||1||
Z||000000||polomeno||03-20-2001||04:18 PM||||Hey guys.. I have a 84 , 4 banger and i'm going to probly have to replace the head gasket .. . now i know that you need to replace the head bolts also.. my car is in another city where it broke down and i need to know what to ask for at the car part place before i go down.. any kinda of specific head bolts??  and how many are there? anything else i should buy?<P>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mark||03-20-2001||04:23 PM||||The head bolts are sold as a set....at least for the 2.8L they are.  Just ask for a head bolt set for your particular engine.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||862M4inCA||03-20-2001||04:58 PM||||the head bolts are also sold as a set for the 2.5 and I believe you can get a head gasket kit with all the gaskets and bolts provided.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cozmo||03-20-2001||08:01 PM||||The bolts are "TTY" which I think means<BR>"torque to yield"<BR>I haven't got a clue as to what that means, maybe someone could shed some light on this...<BR>All I know is you can't re-use the old ones, and with the cost of the gasket it ain't real cheap.  Be sure the head isn't cracked or warped or you get to do the job again as well as pay for parts and head work.<BR>It might be a good idea to have the head done over while it's out if the rest of the engine is in good shape. <BR>I know it's tough when the car is in another city, but you may not have a choice... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Good Luck!<BR>C02M0||||reg||1
Z||000004||862M4inCA||03-20-2001||08:16 PM||||it means that the bolts are torqued to their limit the first time they're used, and as a result if you were to reuse the bolts then you run the risk of breaking the bolt off since it's already been pushed to the bolts torque threshold the first time it was used.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cozmo||03-20-2001||08:27 PM||||I wonder what "The General" had in mind when they used this type instead of regular studs and bolts. It doesn't look like there are any clearance problems and the engine is all cast iron...<BR>Can regular studs and bolts of the correct size and strength be used instead?<BR>C02M0||||reg||1
Z||000006||polomeno||03-20-2001||08:39 PM||||anyone know where in canada i can get the bolts and gasket set?  Will canadian tire sell it?<P>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000007||MrPBody||03-20-2001||08:40 PM||||When I took my head to Dover for a valve job, the counter guy said "I can almost guarantee that it's cracked."  It was. (I saw it.)  Seems to be a common problem.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||862M4inCA||03-20-2001||08:45 PM||||the 4 banger head is notorious for cracking due to a light casting where the steel is sometimes no thicker than 1/4" Most common locations for cracks are typically between the intake and exhaust valve seats. When I had mine magnaflexed it also showed stress cracks at the top of the head where the casting is the thinnest. Needless to say this engine combined with the heat buildup caused by sometimes insufficient airflow around the engine create a bad situation all together.||||reg||1
